# Backend Rules

## Data Access Layer
All Supabase queries must go in `src/services/*.service.ts`:
- Browser client: `createBrowserClient()` for client components
- Server client: `createServerClient()` for Server Components + Server Actions
- Admin client: `createAdminClient()` for privileged operations only

## Service Pattern
```typescript
// Always handle errors; don't expose raw Supabase errors
export const jobService = {
  async getJob(id: string) {
    try {
      const supabase = createBrowserClient();
      const { data, error } = await supabase
        .from('jobs')
        .select('*, organization(*), skills(*)')
        .eq('id', id)
        .single();
      if (error) throw error;
      return data;
    } catch (err) {
      console.error('jobService.getJob:', err);
      return null;
    }
  }
};
```

## Security
- Never bypass RLS (don't use admin client for user-facing queries)
- Always verify auth in Server Actions before any mutation
- Never log sensitive data (passwords, tokens, full session objects)

## Supabase Auth
- Use `createServerClient()` to get user in Server Components
- `const { data: { user } } = await supabase.auth.getUser()`
- Always check `!user` before proceeding with protected operations

## Row-Level Security
All tables MUST have RLS enabled. Check migrations:
- `supabase/` folder contains all migrations
- Test that RLS prevents cross-user access manually

## File Storage
- Avatars: `avatars` bucket (public, max 5MB, images only)
- Resumes: `resumes` bucket (private, max 10MB, PDF only)
- Always sanitize filenames before upload
- Use signed URLs for private content
